 "text": "Hi, how you doing these days? Many areas don't want it down the toilet, so fill up at the office or a bar before heading out. Or see if the campsite has a fill hole. It' still water, and every drop counts somewhere. A fill bottle and an empty tank are the classic signs for a fill site. Some places do ask that, usually with a layer of dirt on top. Check the office website or ask at the site entry. Campsites are shared resources, so they want keep things clean and fair for everyone. You already are, you just didn't realize it.",
